  $ sw_vers
  ProductName:		macOS
  ProductVersion:		26.6.2
  BuildVersion:		25G83

===== Phase 1 — enrolment =====

[1.2] how the machine enrolled — or that it did not
  $ profiles status -type enrollment
  Enrolled via DEP: No
  MDM enrollment: No

[1.4] volume ownership, and the recovery path the machine actually has
  $ fdesetup status
  FileVault is On.
  $ diskutil apfs listCryptoUsers /
  Cryptographic users for disk3s1s1 (2 found)
  |
  +-- <local-user-crypto-uuid>
  |   Type: Local Open Directory User
  |   Volume Owner: Yes
  |
  +-- EBC6C064-0000-11AA-AA11-00306543ECAC
      Type: Personal Recovery User
      Volume Owner: Yes
   

===== Phase 2 — configuration =====

[2.1] the configuration profiles the machine actually carries
  $ profiles list
  There are no configuration profiles installed for user 'lab-user'
  # system scope needs root: sudo profiles list ; a byte-for-byte payload check is
  #   sudo profiles show -output stdout-xml — both empty on an unmanaged machine

===== Phase 3 — software distribution (needs the munki repo reachable) =====

[3.1] the repository is a web server: the directory is closed, a catalog is served
  $ curl -so /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' http://localhost/munki_repo/
  403
  $ curl -so /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' http://localhost/munki_repo/catalogs/all
  200
  $ curl -so /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' http://localhost/munki_repo/catalogs/testing
  200

===== done — read-only; nothing above changed the machine =====
